{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794546065297,"sessionID":"ses_e2cbe000fffeUqJQnXGz6lLg3F","part":{"id":"prt_1d347df910016yqj2pKLkKRg2J","sessionID":"ses_e2cbe000fffeUqJQnXGz6lLg3F","messageID":"msg_1d347d9b60018eU0ydtDJpNQw8","type":"step-start","snapshot":"07fcda692fd031126e4e7a54af5aed8cc5723ebc"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794546073316,"sessionID":"ses_e2cbe000fffeUqJQnXGz6lLg3F","part":{"id":"prt_1d347f0e3002XlBnjKa1CjrebN","sessionID":"ses_e2cbe000fffeUqJQnXGz6lLg3F","messageID":"msg_1d347d9b60018eU0ydtDJpNQw8","type":"text","text":"Done. T010 is complete.\n\n## Files written\n\n**`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs`**\n- `copyVerdict`: before the `if (!exists)` block, returns `{ state: INFO, kind: 'pointer missing', detail: 'Claude Code reads only CLAUDE.md, so without a one-line @' + manifest.root_file + ' pointer it never loads ' + manifest.root_file }` when the path is `CLAUDE.md`, it neither exists nor is a symlink, and `context.exists` is true.\n- `rowRuntimeCopies`: also prints `${path}: ${kind} - ${detail}` when the kind is `pointer missing`. The row-state rule is untouched, so INFO still leaves A10 PASS.\n- Rewrote the A10 comment to say Claude Code reaches the root document only through `CLAUDE.md`, so a missing pointer leaves Claude without it and a full copy double-loads and drifts.\n\n**`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs`**\n- One new case: a `pure` fixture with no `CLAUDE.md` gives the `CLAUDE.md` entry `kind` `pointer missing`, `state` `INFO`, the A10 row `state` `PASS`, and a line starting `CLAUDE.md: pointer missing`.\n\n## Verify output\n\n```\n$ node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs\nℹ tests 40\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 40\nℹ fail 0\n\n$ node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs | rg -c \"^STATUS=OK\"\n1\n```\n\n`node --check` passes on both files. The diff is confined to those two files.\n\n## One thing worth knowing\n\nThe `pure` fixture alone reports A10 `FINDING`, unrelated to this change: `compose-fixture.cjs` writes only the Gate 1 mirror, while `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --check` now also requires the Gate 2 command block. So the case runs the sync's own writer once on the temp tree (`spawnSync ... --root <fixture>`) to make the tree the one a repository that ran its generators carries. Without that step the requested `A10` `PASS` assertion is unreachable on any throwaway tree. The composer is not named by this task, so I left it alone, but it is behind its generator.","time":{"start":1794546069731,"end":1794546073316}}}
